     %%%    L o o p m a r k   L e g e n d    %%%

     Primary Loop Type        Modifiers
     ------- ---- ----        ---------
     There are no optimizations or loops to mark


    1.          FUNCTION J4SAVE(IWHICH,IVALUE,ISET)
    2.    C***BEGIN PROLOGUE  J4SAVE
    3.    C***REFER TO  XERROR
    4.    C     Abstract
    5.    C        J4SAVE saves and recalls several global variables needed
    6.    C        by the library error handling routines.
    7.    C
    8.    C     Description of Parameters
    9.    C      --Input--
   10.    C        IWHICH - Index of item desired.
   11.    C                = 1 Refers to current error number.
   12.    C                = 2 Refers to current error control flag.
   13.    C                 = 3 Refers to current unit number to which error
   14.    C                    messages are to be sent.  (0 means use standard.)
   15.    C                 = 4 Refers to the maximum number of times any
   16.    C                     message is to be printed (as set by XERMAX).
   17.    C                 = 5 Refers to the total number of units to which
   18.    C                     each error message is to be written.
   19.    C                 = 6 Refers to the 2nd unit for error messages
   20.    C                 = 7 Refers to the 3rd unit for error messages
   21.    C                 = 8 Refers to the 4th unit for error messages
   22.    C                 = 9 Refers to the 5th unit for error messages
   23.    C        IVALUE - The value to be set for the IWHICH-th parameter,
   24.    C                 if ISET is .TRUE. .
   25.    C        ISET   - If ISET=.TRUE., the IWHICH-th parameter will BE
   26.    C                 given the value, IVALUE.  If ISET=.FALSE., the
   27.    C                 IWHICH-th parameter will be unchanged, and IVALUE
   28.    C                 is a dummy parameter.
   29.    C      --Output--
   30.    C        The (old) value of the IWHICH-th parameter will be returned
   31.    C        in the function value, J4SAVE.
   32.    C
   33.    C     Written by Ron Jones, with SLATEC Common Math Library Subcommittee
   34.    C    Adapted from Bell Laboratories PORT Library Error Handler
   35.    C     Latest revision ---  23 MAY 1979
   36.    C***REFERENCES  JONES R.E., KAHANER D.K., "XERROR, THE SLATEC ERROR-
   37.    C                 HANDLING PACKAGE", SAND82-0800, SANDIA LABORATORIES,
   38.    C                 1982.
   39.    C***ROUTINES CALLED  (NONE)
   40.    C***END PROLOGUE  J4SAVE
   41.          LOGICAL ISET
   42.          INTEGER IPARAM(9)
   43.          SAVE IPARAM
   44.          DATA IPARAM(1),IPARAM(2),IPARAM(3),IPARAM(4)/0,2,0,10/
   45.          DATA IPARAM(5)/1/
   46.          DATA IPARAM(6),IPARAM(7),IPARAM(8),IPARAM(9)/0,0,0,0/
   47.    C***FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  J4SAVE
   48.          J4SAVE = IPARAM(IWHICH)
   49.          IF (ISET) IPARAM(IWHICH) = IVALUE
   50.          RETURN
   51.          END


